+# Native Master defaults
+
+An authored structured workspace can provide `templates/master_defaults.json` to create editable Master placeholders and sparse Layout/Slide defaults. The builder consumes the profile during package assembly. The same builder serves template preview and project export. A workspace without the file uses the existing export path. Mirror, source-preserve, flat, and round-trip exports do not accept this profile.
+
+The profile must declare every Master, Layout, and slot in the active roster, including retained Layout prototypes. Unknown schema keys, missing slots, unsupported property names, escaping snippet paths, and unsupported XML fail export. The existing template installer carries the JSON and XML snippets with the structure owner's snapshot.
+
+## Profile structure
+
+```json
+{
+  "schema": "ppt-master.master-defaults.v1",
+  "masters": {
+    "main": {
+      "placeholders": {
+        "title": "master-defaults/title.xml",
+        "body": "master-defaults/body.xml",
+        "date": "master-defaults/date.xml",
+        "footer": "master-defaults/footer.xml",
+        "slide-number": "master-defaults/slide-number.xml"
+      },
+      "text_styles": "master-defaults/text-styles.xml"
+    }
+  },
+  "policies": {
+    "ordinary-title": {
+      "geometry": "inherit",
+      "body_properties": "master-defaults/empty-body.xml",
+      "list_style": "master-defaults/empty-list.xml",
+      "slide_inherits": ["geometry", "body.insets", "body.anchor", "body.layout", "text.size", "text.faces", "text.bold", "text.italic", "text.color", "text.decoration", "text.tracking", "text.baseline", "paragraph.spacing", "paragraph.list", "paragraph.align"]
+    }
+  },
+  "layouts": {
+    "content": {
+      "master": "main",
+      "slots": {"title-slot": "ordinary-title"},
+      "optional_date_idx": 9,
+      "color_map": "master-defaults/dark-map.xml"
+    }
+  },
+  "preview_anchors": {
+    "title": {"layout": "content", "slot": "title-slot"},
+    "body": {"layout": "content", "slot": "body-slot"}
+  }
+}
+```
+
+The example abbreviates the slot roster. `preview_anchors` is optional and reads provisional pixel sizes from two SVG text carriers. It affects template preview only. Project export uses its supplied `MasterTextStyleSpec`. Optional `preview_colors` supplies the four provisional `dk1`, `dk2`, `lt1`, and `lt2` RGB slots to template preview only. Ordinary project export never consumes this preview palette.
+
+Each Master snippet has a `p:sp` root and the corresponding native `p:ph` type: `title`, `body`, `dt`, `ftr`, or `sldNum`. Shape IDs are assigned by the builder. The `p:txStyles` snippet must include title level 1 and body/other levels 1–9. Text size parameters are `sz="${title_hpt}"` and `sz="${body_hpt}"`. They resolve to hundredths of a point from the current project. Bind each body level to the same body parameter to preserve size while levels change indentation and bullets.
+
+Snippets are relationship-free XML fragments inside `templates/`. They cannot contain media, links, themes, extension payloads, external entities, or arbitrary OOXML. Font faces use `+mj-*` / `+mn-*`; colors use theme roles or neutral black, white, and gray. Brand resources own the full theme and concrete fonts. Optional `color_bindings` maps each named parameter to a project color role and a neutral grayscale fallback. For example, `"footer_light": {"role": "footer_light", "fallback": "666666"}` permits `<a:srgbClr val="${color.footer_light}"/>`. The builder resolves these from the original `ThemeColorSpec.roles` before binding the Brand theme, so colors outside the twelve theme slots remain available. The neutral Layout contains no brand RGB. Only named color parameters on `a:srgbClr@val` accept this substitution. A Layout can supply a `p:clrMapOvr` snippet to choose how that theme's roles map on dark or light backgrounds.
+
+Master and Layout entries can optionally name a `background` XML snippet. Its `p:bg` contains either a solid `p:bgPr` using `bg1`/`bg2`, or `p:bgRef` with index 1001–1003 and one untransformed `bg1`/`bg2` color. The SVG must still declare the corresponding background as its visual fallback. The materializer preserves the native theme alias and background-style reference, and validates the resulting package against that snippet.
+
+A policy's `geometry` controls Layout ownership. `inherit` omits Layout `a:xfrm`; `svg-bounds` writes the declared slot bounds. `body_properties` and `list_style` are sparse `a:bodyPr` and `a:lstStyle` fragments. Empty fragments inherit. The builder does not fill them with Office defaults or infer them from the first content run.
+
+`slide_inherits` controls each property's removal from Slide-local output. Supported groups are shown above. Individual run names are `size`, `bold`, `italic`, `color`, `latin`, `ea`, `cs`, `underline`, `strike`, `tracking`, and `baseline`. Individual paragraph names are `line-spacing`, `space-before`, `space-after`, `bullet`, `indent`, and `align`. Property equality never establishes ownership.
+
+Native chart/table content remains owned by those objects. Their graphic-frame geometry is mandatory OOXML and must remain local. Give such slots an empty `slide_inherits`. Picture slots can inherit geometry; the builder retains the converter's contained image area by adjusting `a:fillRect` before removing the Slide frame.
+
+## Content and local overrides
+
+Every text carrier under this profile declares `data-pptx-native-defaults="true"`. Carrier appearance remains a full SVG preview fallback. A carrier can declare `data-pptx-local="size,color"` to retain specific local overrides. Nested `tspan`/link style declarations also establish local ownership, including a declaration equal to the inherited value. Explicit normal/none/zero values emit actual reset attributes.
+
+When a primary language is supplied, the same shared language binder updates both compiled default snippets and the exported package. Validation still checks every expected attribute; it does not discard language differences.
+
+The converter retains this ownership through run coalescing. It emits temporary `data-pptx-local` attributes on `a:rPr` and `a:pPr`; the builder consumes and removes them before package validation. Missing provenance on a managed text run is an error. It never clears an entire `rPr`, text body, hyperlink, language, or field identity to create inheritance.
+
+Use `data-pptx-level="0"` through `"8"` on semantic paragraph tspans. Preserve existing `data-paragraph-space-before` / `data-paragraph-space-after` intent, including zero. Pixel paragraph spacing converts to points. `data-pptx-bullet="none"` or a single character and `data-pptx-indent` / `data-pptx-margin-left` provide explicit paragraph overrides. A slot-level `data-pptx-local="geometry"` preserves a Slide-local frame. Default profile text flow is `preserve`, so semantic paragraphs stay in one native carrier.
+
+A Layout footer uses the prototype's actual footer text as its new-slide default. An empty footer stays empty. Title and body placeholders keep editing prompts rather than inheriting prototype content.
+
+`optional_date_idx` adds a native date placeholder to the Layout but no Slide object. It must not collide with a declared slot. The Layout keeps `p:hf@dt=0`. An optional `optional_date_policy` names the sparse body/text policy for this native-only slot, for example a dark-background field color; its geometry must inherit. A real declared date slot, such as cover content, remains present. Slide-number slots always contain `a:fld type="slidenum"`, including neutral preview. Optional date capability uses `datetime1`.
+
+## Verification
+
+Package validation retains the existing part/relationship, content-type, name, slot, background, and ID checks. Profile slots additionally check effective Master→Layout→Slide bounds, declared sparse Layout defaults, missing local geometry where inheritance is required, absence of undeclared local run defaults, automatic page-number fields, and removal of converter metadata. The template checker loads the same profile before export.
+
+From the oracle-template-installer skill directory, run its distributed verifier:
+
+```sh
+python3 -B scripts/verify_runtime.py qualify --work /absolute/new-check --report /absolute/report.json
+```
+
+XML and python-pptx tests prove package structure and supported effective-value resolution. PowerPoint's new-slide, Master-edit, date enablement, reset/layout switching, and save/reopen behavior still require native application verification.
