 ```
 
 Derives the index entry from `templates/design_spec.md` (frontmatter preferred; prose fallback) plus the actual `templates/*.svg` roster and updates `templates/brands/brands_index.json`, `styles/styles_index.json`, `layouts/layouts_index.json`, or `decks/decks_index.json`. The JSON index is the single discovery source for Default Stage-1 template controls and chat listing; READMEs describe kinds in prose and are never edited. `--dry-run` checks the directory/index identity without writing.
+
+
+## Explicit native Master defaults
+
+Authored structured workspaces may provide `templates/master_defaults.json` for five native Master roles, sparse per-property inheritance, and optional date capability. See [Native Master defaults](native-master-defaults.md) for the profile and SVG metadata contract. Workspaces without this profile keep the existing behavior.
+
+
+## Portable Brand assets and image backgrounds
+
+A selected Brand may provide `templates/brand_assets.json`:
+
+```json
+{
+  "schema": "ppt-master.brand-assets.v1",
+  "assets": {
+    "cover-background": {"path": "images/cover.jpg", "sha256": "<64 lowercase hex characters>"},
+    "wordmark-on-dark": {"path": "images/wordmark.svg", "sha256": "<64 lowercase hex characters>"}
+  },
+  "colors": {"cover-accent": "#F0CC72"}
+}
+```
+
+`assets` maps semantic roles to workspace-relative local files and their SHA-256
+hashes. `colors` is optional. Paths must stay under `images/` within the Brand
+workspace, including after resolving symlinks. URLs and escaping paths fail.
+
+An authored Layout declares `data-pptx-brand-asset="cover-background"` on an
+ordinary image with a neutral `href`, or `data-pptx-brand-fill="cover-accent"`
+on an element with a `fill` attribute. The installer binds the selected Brand
+into copied SVG bytes, retaining IDs, geometry, and role declarations. It writes
+image references relative to each installed SVG. The manifest and image files
+enter the installation receipt as Brand metadata/assets; they do not become
+Layout roster entries. Source SVG hashes remain separate from installed hashes.
+No manifest leaves the neutral SVG unchanged. A present manifest with a missing
+requested role fails. Repeat installation from unchanged roots is idempotent.
+In-place templates may be reused only when binding would not change their bytes;
+otherwise install the neutral source Layout into a fresh project.
+
+For a native Master/Layout image background, declare a direct `<image>` with
+`data-pptx-background="image"`, `data-pptx-layer="master"` or `"layout"`,
+`preserveAspectRatio="none"`, and exact full-canvas bounds. This contract supports
+uncropped stretch without transforms, filters, opacity, clipping, or hidden
+paint. The exporter moves the compiled picture fill and media relationships to
+`p:cSld/p:bg/p:bgPr/a:blipFill` and removes the duplicate picture. Ordinary
+full-canvas images remain pictures. An explicit image background conflicts with
+a `master_defaults.json` background snippet for the same scope. Authored Brand
+binding and image-background markers are unsupported in source-preserve, mirror,
+and roundtrip exports; an unused installed manifest alone does not trigger that
+restriction.
